# What the GitNexus code-graph indexer must NOT ingest (WI-6445).
#
# gitnexus reads .gitignore, which is not enough here: this tree TRACKS a large
# amount of build output and binary seed data, and a first `npx gitnexus analyze`
# spent its whole run enumerating those rather than source. Everything below is
# either generated, vendored, binary, or a verbatim copy of source indexed
# elsewhere — none of it is a symbol anyone will ever look up.
#
# Regenerate the index with: npx gitnexus analyze . --skip-agents-md --name papercusp
# (--skip-agents-md is REQUIRED: the default rewrites a section into the shared
# CLAUDE.md / AGENTS.md, which are prompt SOURCES in this repo.)

# Binary seed corestore + hypercore blobs (tracked, ~thousands of .blob/.sst).
papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/seed/
**/corestore/

# Built SPA bundles + the composed sidecar, including its verbatim COPIES of the
# prompts tree and all db migrations — indexing these double-counts every symbol.
papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/sidecar/
papercusp-desktop/src-tauri/env-sidecars/
**/spa/assets/
**/storybook-static/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.next/
**/out/

# Retired-but-preserved surfaces: deliberately not deployed and not to be
# extended (see CLAUDE.md § retired surfaces). A code-graph hit here would point
# an agent at code the repo forbids wiring into.
_retired/
**/_retired/

# Vendored / generated / non-source.
**/node_modules/
**/.venv/
**/target/
**/*.min.js
**/*.map
**/coverage/
